                <pb facs="0704" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg696"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.71/151a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gunther</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-10-13T18:00:00-05:00">October 13, 1939—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>186. Authoritative Polish military personage recently in Rumania states in Paris
                    that Rumania is now filled with OGPU and Gestapo agents. He recently observed
                    large concentration of Soviet troops in Polish territory on northern Rumania
                    frontiers. He is convinced that a Soviet entry into Rumania will follow the
                    present Finnish crisis.</p>
                <p>The Polish Ambassador in Paris believes that a Soviet attack on Rumania or the
                    entry of Russian troops into the country with the consent of the Rumanian
                    Government would result in murder of members of the former Polish Government by
                    either the OGPU or the Gestapo.</p>
                <p>Is Moscicki still in Rumania?</p>
                <p>Please comment on the foregoing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
